      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753574400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "20 IOPS/TB = f4 migration trigger \u00b7 a 4TB drive safely handles ~80 IOPS/TB",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "20 IOPS/TB = f4 migration trigger \u00b7 a 4TB drive safely handles ~80 IOPS/TB",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b_mismatch",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 500,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 110,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#b45309",
      "backgroundColor": "#fffbeb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "t_mismatch",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1753574400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t_mismatch",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 512,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 86,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#78350f",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753574400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "THE MISMATCH\nHaystack replicated every object 3.6x \u2014 three full geographic copies \u00d7 1.2 for RAID-6 \u2014 no matter whether it was read a thousand times a day or once a year. Durability and throughput were the same number: an old photo couldn't get less redundancy without also getting less durability.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "b_mismatch",
      "originalText": "THE MISMATCH\nHaystack replicated every object 3.6x \u2014 three full geographic copies \u00d7 1.2 for RAID-6 \u2014 no matter whether it was read a thousand times a day or once a year. Durability and throughput were the same number: an old photo couldn't get less redundancy without also getting less durability.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b_changed",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 625,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 130,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4338ca",
      "backgroundColor": "#eef2ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "t_changed",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1753574400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t_changed",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 637,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 106,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#312e81",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753574400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHAT CHANGED\nf4 decouples them. Reed-Solomon(10,4) erasure-codes each stripe \u2014 10 data blocks, 4 parity blocks, spread across racks \u2014 for 1.4x local overhead instead of 3x, same failure tolerance. A geo-mirrored copy in a second datacenter brings it to 2.8x; XOR-coding the two datacenters' encoded copies against each other cuts it to 2.1x, still surviving a full datacenter loss. A router tracks trailing IOPS/TB per volume and migrates it once it crosses the line.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "b_changed",
      "originalText": "WHAT CHANGED\nf4 decouples them. Reed-Solomon(10,4) erasure-codes each stripe \u2014 10 data blocks, 4 parity blocks, spread across racks \u2014 for 1.4x local overhead instead of 3x, same failure tolerance. A geo-mirrored copy in a second datacenter brings it to 2.8x; XOR-coding the two datacenters' encoded copies against each other cuts it to 2.1x, still surviving a full datacenter loss. A router tracks trailing IOPS/TB per volume and migrates it once it crosses the line.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "e_footnote",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 775,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#334155",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753574400000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Haystack wasn't a bad design \u2014 it was tuned for the exact shape of the corpus in 2008, when almost every stored photo had just been uploaded. The problem was quieter: one replication number was being asked to answer two different questions for six years after the corpus's shape had already changed underneath it.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Haystack wasn't a bad design \u2014 it was tuned for the exact shape of the corpus in 2008, when almost every stored photo had just been uploaded. The problem was quieter: one replication number was being asked to answer two different questions for six years after the corpus's shape had already changed underneath it.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
